---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const steps = [
  ['1', 'Understand the idea', '/en/essays/idea-5min', 'Persistence is what passes through a constraint without losing structural identity.'],
  ['2', 'State the principle', '/en/premier-principe', 'GFT fixes the budget: total distinction = persistence + entropy.'],
  ['3', 'See one proof route', '/en/tableau-periodique', 'The periodic table gives a robust, visual, chemical first demonstration.'],
  ['4', 'Compare with measurements', '/en/resultats', 'Numerical results are grouped by domain, status, and validation level.'],
  ['5', 'Inspect the limits', '/en/limites', 'A credible theory must state what is proved, derived, validated, or still open.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Start here"
  description="Guided route for reading the Theory of Persistence in the right order."
>
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <p class="pt-tag pt-tag-bridge mb-4">Guided route</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-thmblue mb-5">Start here</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-10">
      The site has many entry points. This page gives the recommended order:
      first the principle, then a readable demonstration, then results,
      epistemic status, and limits.
    </p>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-5 gap-3 mb-12">
      {steps.map(([num, title, href, text]) => (
        <a href={href} class="pt-card block group">
          <span class="text-sm font-mono text-derorange">{num}</span>
          <h2 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue text-xl mt-2 mb-2 group-hover:underline">{title}</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">{text}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] gap-8 items-start">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-thmblue mb-3">The through-line</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          PT does not begin with a constant to tune. It begins with a
          conservation constraint: a system has a total budget of distinctions.
          That budget may appear as persistent structure or as entropic
          dispersion, but the balance is exact.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
          The scientific question then becomes: does this conservation force
          recognizable structures in the world? The first robust showcase is
          chemical: periods, channels, shells, then IE and EA.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
        <h2 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue text-xl mb-3">Recommended 20-minute route</h2>
        <ol class="space-y-3 text-slate-700">
          <li><strong>5 min.</strong> Read “The idea in 5 minutes”.</li>
          <li><strong>5 min.</strong> Read “Fundamental principle” in L1 mode.</li>
          <li><strong>7 min.</strong> Read the periodic-table demonstration.</li>
          <li><strong>3 min.</strong> Open the results dashboard and limits page.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
